   "description": [
    "November 15 1913 BALTIMORE COUNTY Regular Monthly Meeting Held at Mt Washington The regular monthly meeting of the Just Government League of Bal timore County was held on November io at the residence of Mrs Town send Scott at Mt Washington It was reported that a large amount of literature was distributed at the polls on November 4 and that a quantity of it was placed in the leading stores postoffice and railroad station Plans were made for an evening meeting at the Casino some time during the month the purpose of whcih is to interest the workers in the Mt Washington mills At the close of the business meeting Miss Katherine McCormick who has done settlement work in Chicago gave a most interesting talk followed by some remarks from Dr Mary Sherwood Helen E Scott ELECTION DAY IN CENTERVILLE Distribution of Literature at Polls a Feature Election day was very quiet at Centerville although some little stir was noticeable when Miss L C Trax carrying a white canvas bag marked Votes for Women appeared on the bank corner and began distributing suffrage literature A small crowd soon collected and Miss Trax was kept busy answering questions and discussing the"
