   "description": [
    "WOMAN SUFFRAGE YEAR BOOR THE Suffrage Year Book for 1917 so anxiously awaited is off the press It is by far the most ambitious effort suffragists have as yet made in the matter of year books It is by no means easy to issue under one cover illuminating information on Suffrage Events in 1916 Suffrage History Arguments Statistics Charts Bibliography International Alli ance Federal Amendment Presidential Suffrage State Referenda Lists of Associations in the United States Suffrage Planks in Party Platforms Effect of Woman Suffrage Number of Women Voters Laws Affecting Women and Children Persons Excluded from Suffrage Jury Service and Poll Tax Facts for Suffrage Workers Sentiment in Favor Cost of Elec tions as we were saying it is by no means easy to do it But it has been done In the result the National Woman Suffrage Publishing Co is offer ing a limited edition of this very substantial volume at 105 postpaid It is edited by Martha G Stapler THE LESLIE WOMAN SUFFRAGE COMMISSION UNDER a recent court ruling an order of distribution of a portion of the Leslie fortune left to Mrs Catt for use in suffrage work has been issued This does not mean however"
