   "description": [
    "A PRIMER OF DEMOCRACY or AN EXPOSITION OF SUFFRAGE AND ITS OUTLOOK Continued from last week 21 After the fall of the Roman Empire and before the beginning of the modern States of Europe did suffrage exist Europe entered upon and continued from the fall of the Roman Empire in 476 A D to 1492 A D the discovery of the new world in what is known as the Middle Ages a thousand years During this period from the tenth century onward the feudal ages prevailed During this era suffrage as a popular question is very obscure 22 Can we discern any movements toward suffrage in the Middle Ages that is prior to the discovery of the new world Among the AngloSaxons the folkmote or peoples meetings was a kind of town meeting the witenagemot or assembly of the wise was a general or national parliament Habeas corpus and trial by jury existed in the common law The rise of the free cities of Europe in connection with commerce and guilds or associations of an industrial religious or other kind furnish examples of a tendency toward modern suffrage Among other examples of the extension of human rights may be named"
   ],
