   "description": [
    "108 CHAMP CLARK FOR WOMAN SUFFRAGE National Congressional Committee Presents Petition to CongressVicePresi dent Courteous But NonCommittal Suffrage scored a great victory on Saturday June 27 when Hon Champ Clark Speaker of the House of Representatives announced that when woman suffrage was submitted in Missouri he would vote for it To have the second officer in power in the National Government thus declare himself in such a pronounced manner as favoring woman suffrage was well worth the assembling of the prominent women in Washington at that time The occasion was the presentation of the petitions of the May 2 demonstration to the Congress of the United States by the National Congressional Committee The delegation which assembled in the Speakers room consisted of Dr Anna Howard Shaw of Philadelphia president of the National Woman Suffrage Association Miss Jane Addams of Chicago first vicepresident Mrs Desha Breckenridge sec ond vicepresident Mrs Medill McCormick of Chicago chairman of the Congressional Committee of the National Association Mrs An toinette Funk of Chicago vicechairman of the Congressional Com mittee Mrs Helen Gardener of Washington another member of the committee Mrs Glenna Smith Tinnin of Washington chairman of the Washington Woman Suffrage Council and Mrs Raymond"
