   "description": [
    "162 for over onehalf of the voters of the State have voiced their own de mand in this regard The Next Step There is no doubt but that a large proportion of the members of the Democratic party wish to have a suffrage referendum plank inserted in the party platform The leaders can however make it exceedingly difficult for the people to secure this plank by appointing an adverse platform committee The only way to insure the insertion of the suf frage referendum plank is to make it clear to the Democratic leaders that suffrage sentiment is so strong in the State that the omission of the plank would be detrimental to the party in the November elections Expediency is a singularly powerful factor in political circles Jus tice fades into insignificance beside it It may be doubted whether even the Republican party would have inserted the suffrage plank if the leaders had believed it would be inexpedient to do so The chief work for the present then is to convince the Democratic leaders of the expe diency of inserting the suffrage plank and of the dangerous inexpediency of omitting it Here again the only ammunition the suffragists have is"
   ],
