   "description": [
    "A PRIMER OF DEMOCRACY or AN EXPOSITION OF SUFFRAGE AND ITS OUTLOOK Continued from last week 57 But do not men who are heads of families have suffrage and thus represent their families As has been said the representative idea has dropped out of suffrage which has become individualistic the family therefore has no direct part in government under individualistic suffrage 58 Can you illustrate this defect as you term it Here are two men one has no family whatever the other has a family of one or more children Both have the same suffrage I maintain that the former represents suffrage reduced to its lowest terms and that here the family as such is unrepresented and has no direct share in govern ment and that it lacks the advantages for which suffrage stands Suf frage as a direct issue is strictly individualistic 59 What then do you propose I propose the triple ballot instead of the single or dual ballot that is both the individual and the family with minor offspring shall have suf frage or in other words male female and family with minor off spring or household suffrage 60 Would you give the family a vote in"
